					<p>Birthdate: June 3, 1919</p>
<p>URS May 31, 2011</p>
<p>Khair-un-nisa was born on June 3, 1919, the youngest child of Pir-o-Murshid Hazrat Inayat Khan and Ameena Begum.  The name Claire was given to her by her older sister Noor-un-nisa.  In her  early years, Claire trained as a pianist and studied  musical composition under Nadia Boulanger in Paris. As the Second World War approached, Claire studied nursing  and during World War II  she worked in British hospitals. Following the war, Claire  moved between the United States and Europe while working and raising  her son David Inayat Harper.</p>
<p>In her later years, Claire wrote her memories of life in the Inayat Khan family. Her memoir, <strong><em>&#8220;We Rubies Four&#8221;</em></strong> was published by Omega Publications in 2011.</p>
	
				       				
																					
				</div>
		
