	<h3 id="comments">2 Memories for &#8220;Khair-un-nisa &#8220;Claire&#8221; Inayat Khan&#8221;</h3> 

	<ol class="commentlist">
						<li class="alt" id="comment-11636">
			<div class="cmtinfo"><em> on 22 Apr 2012 at 11:13 am</em><small class="commentmetadata"><a href="index.html?p=822#comment-11636" title=""><span class="commentnum">1</span></a></small><cite>Imam Salim Chishti</cite></div>
						
			<p>I remember when she lived at the Abode of the Message for a short while, my friend and I would drive her to the doctor&#8217;s office occasionally. Such a sweet soul, delicate. The fragrance of her essence was always with her, and always brightened the drive. I don&#8217;t have much more to say other then it was truly a blessing to have known her.</p>
			
		</li>

	
					<li class="" id="comment-32783">
			<div class="cmtinfo"><em> on 07 Sep 2014 at 12:06 pm</em><small class="commentmetadata"><a href="index.html?p=822#comment-32783" title=""><span class="commentnum">2</span></a></small><cite><a href='http://theunsuperheroes.blogspot.ca/' rel='external nofollow' class='url'>michael marshall</a></cite></div>
						
			<p>Claire was also a pioneer in growing penicillin &#8211; being one of the first two women ever permitted to enter the august walls of Sir Howard Florey&#8217;s Dunn institute at highly old fashioned Oxford university !</p>
			
		</li>

	
	
	</ol>

